(Relational Databases - Task Answers) Tj T*
(=====================================) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. What is normalisation?) Tj T*
(=========================) Tj T*
(Normalisation is the process of restructuring database tables to reduce data) Tj T*
(redundancy and eliminate data anomalies. The goal is to bring the database to) Tj T*
(a consistent state where each table represents a single subject, no data is) Tj T*
(unnecessarily duplicated across tables, and all attributes in a table are) Tj T*
(functionally dependent on the primary key. Normalisation works through a series) Tj T*
(of stages called normal forms \(1NF, 2NF, 3NF\), with each stage being) Tj T*
(structurally better than the previous one.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. When is a table in 1NF \(First Normal Form\)?) Tj T*
(===============================================) Tj T*
(A table is in First Normal Form \(1NF\) when:) Tj T*
(- All of the key attributes are defined \(a primary key exists\),) Tj T*
(- There are no repeating groups in the table \(each cell contains a single) Tj T*
(  value, not a list of values\), and) Tj T*
(- All attributes are dependent on the primary key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In other words, data must be presented in a tabular format where each cell) Tj T*
(contains exactly one value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. When is a table in 2NF \(Second Normal Form\)?) Tj T*
(================================================) Tj T*
(A table is in Second Normal Form \(2NF\) when:) Tj T*
(- It is already in 1NF, and) Tj T*
(- It includes no partial dependencies -- that is, no non-key attribute is) Tj T*
(  dependent on only a portion of the primary key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2NF is only relevant when a table has a composite primary key \(a key made up) Tj T*
(of two or more columns\). If the primary key is a single column, a table in) Tj T*
(1NF is automatically in 2NF.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. When is a table in 3NF \(Third Normal Form\)?) Tj T*
(===============================================) Tj T*
(A table is in Third Normal Form \(3NF\) when:) Tj T*
(- It is already in 2NF, and) Tj T*
(- It contains no transitive dependencies -- that is, no non-key attribute is) Tj T*
(  dependent on another non-key attribute.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 3NF, every non-key attribute must depend directly and only on the primary) Tj T*
(key, not on any other non-key column.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=============================================================) Tj T*
(INVOICE TABLE ANALYSIS \(Questions 5, 6, and 7\)) Tj T*
(=============================================================) Tj T*
ET
endstream
